00:17:50.140 --> 00:17:55.760
just because imagine a scenario where it's, like, the floating 1P over your head,

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.560
and you have to hit, like, select to change between the two.

00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:03.540
So we've seen that in, like, ways to control football teams in NES games,

00:18:03.680 --> 00:18:09.420
or even just other video games where, like, you switch between which character you want to play before the hike, right?

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:12.640
It wouldn't work here in this volleyball game,

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:16.400
and so I kind of, I never really considered the other option until Sean brought it up,

00:18:16.520 --> 00:18:20.840
that, like, there could be a world where you just play as one of them and the computer is the other,

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:25.580
and that would feel really bad when the computer messes it up because you have no role in that,

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.260
and shouldn't the computer just be perfect?

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:31.520
Perfect. So I think it's really smart of them, in the long run,

00:18:31.640 --> 00:18:34.720
especially knowing how twitch reflexy the game gets,

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:39.500
that it's worth it so that the game kind of decides for you, like, who you are.

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:42.880
